function nipunaPage(){return pageHero('NIPUNA | Life skills programme','Beyond technical skills. Building life skills.','A structured 120-hour life skills programme that complements technical training. Across 10 learning modules, NIPUNA helps participants strengthen communication, confidence, personal development and the practical behaviours that support a positive transition into work.')+
'<section class="section"><div class="wrap nipuna-intro"><div class="nipuna-visual reveal"><div class="floating-stat"><strong>120 hours</strong><small>A structured learning experience across 10 modules</small></div></div><div class="reveal"><span class="eyebrow">The NIPUNA programme</span><h2>Skills for work. Confidence for life.</h2><p>Technical knowledge is only one part of becoming work-ready. People also need to communicate clearly, work with others, manage everyday responsibilities and approach new situations with confidence.</p><p>NIPUNA is Hill Green Techno Solutions’ life skills programme. It is designed to complement technical and vocational learning, helping participants build the personal and interpersonal capabilities they can carry into the workplace and everyday life.</p><div class="nipuna-points"><span>Personal development</span><span>Communication</span><span>Workplace readiness</span><span>Employability skills</span></div></div></div></section>'+
'<section class="section soft"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-head"><span class="eyebrow">Programme at a glance</span><h2>A clear structure. A practical purpose.</h2><p>NIPUNA is designed as a structured programme that can sit alongside technical training and broader skill development initiatives.</p></div><div class="nipuna-stats-grid"><article class="nipuna-stat-card"><strong>120</strong><span>Programme hours</span><small>Structured learning time</small></article><article class="nipuna-stat-card"><strong>10</strong><span>Learning modules</span><small>Progressive learning structure</small></article><article class="nipuna-stat-card"><strong>1:50</strong><span>Documented trainer ratio</span><small>Programme planning reference</small></article><article class="nipuna-stat-card"><strong>360°</strong><span>Whole-person development</span><small>Personal, social and work-related skills</small></article></div></div></section>'+
'<section class="section"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-head"><span class="eyebrow">Learning areas</span><h2>Ten themes that connect learning with everyday life.</h2><p>The themes below describe the capabilities NIPUNA is designed to strengthen. They are presented as learning areas, not as the official titles of the programme’s 10 curriculum modules.</p></div><div class="nipuna-modules">'+
'<article class="nipuna-module"><span>01</span><div><h3>Self-awareness and personal growth</h3><p>Recognise personal strengths, understand areas for development and set meaningful goals.</p></div></article>'+
'<article class="nipuna-module"><span>02</span><div><h3>Effective communication</h3><p>Share ideas clearly, listen actively and communicate respectfully in different situations.</p></div></article>'+
'<article class="nipuna-module"><span>03</span><div><h3>Interpersonal relationships</h3><p>Build positive relationships, show respect and respond constructively to different perspectives.</p></div></article>'+
'<article class="nipuna-module"><span>04</span><div><h3>Teamwork and collaboration</h3><p>Contribute to shared tasks, understand responsibilities and work towards common goals.</p></div></article>'+
'<article class="nipuna-module"><span>05</span><div><h3>Confidence and positive attitude</h3><p>Develop confidence, take initiative and approach challenges with a willingness to learn.</p></div></article>'+
'<article class="nipuna-module"><span>06</span><div><h3>Problem-solving and decision-making</h3><p>Think through everyday challenges, consider options and make responsible decisions.</p></div></article>'+
'<article class="nipuna-module"><span>07</span><div><h3>Time management and work discipline</h3><p>Plan tasks, manage time, meet commitments and understand the value of consistency.</p></div></article>'+
'<article class="nipuna-module"><span>08</span><div><h3>Professional behaviour and workplace etiquette</h3><p>Understand workplace expectations, professional conduct and respectful interactions.</p></div></article>'+
'<article class="nipuna-module"><span>09</span><div><h3>Employability and interview readiness</h3><p>Present skills and experience, prepare for opportunities and communicate strengths.</p></div></article>'+
'<article class="nipuna-module"><span>10</span><div><h3>Workplace readiness and adaptability</h3><p>Prepare to learn on the job, respond to change and take responsibility for continued growth.</p></div></article>'+
'</div><p class="nipuna-note">The learning areas are an editorial overview. Final module names, sequence and session-wise hours should follow the approved NIPUNA curriculum.</p></div></section>'+
'<section class="section soft"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-head"><span class="eyebrow">How learning comes to life</span><h2>Learn it. Practise it. Use it.</h2><p>Life skills become meaningful when participants can connect ideas with real situations. NIPUNA’s learning approach can bring concepts to life through guided discussion, individual reflection and practical group activities.</p></div><div class="nipuna-delivery-grid"><article><span>01</span><h3>Understand</h3><p>Introduce a skill, explore why it matters and connect it to everyday or workplace situations.</p></article><article><span>02</span><h3>Practise</h3><p>Use activities, discussion and realistic scenarios to explore how the skill works in practice.</p></article><article><span>03</span><h3>Reflect</h3><p>Review what worked, identify areas to improve and consider how to apply the learning.</p></article></div></div></section>'+
'<section class="section"><div class="wrap nipuna-audience"><div><span class="eyebrow">Who it supports</span><h2>Building the human skills behind employability.</h2><p>NIPUNA is designed to complement technical and vocational training for young people preparing to enter or progress in the world of work. It can also be considered by organisations and programme partners looking to strengthen the life skills component of their training initiatives.</p></div><div class="nipuna-audience-list"><div><b>For participants</b><p>Build confidence, communication and practical skills for work and daily life.</p></div><div><b>For training providers</b><p>Add a structured life skills component alongside technical learning.</p></div><div><b>For programme partners</b><p>Explore a collaborative approach to integrating life skills into workforce development.</p></div></div></div></section>'+
cta('Make life skills part of the journey.','Talk to Hill Green about NIPUNA, programme delivery and potential training partnerships.','Enquire about NIPUNA')}
